From 43823af6871ce18923a69aa4af2487450a0ce01f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kulesha Evgeniy <voovdop@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:12:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] turnip/a5xx: expose samplerAnisotropy for vkmark

The a5xx compute-MVP feature set intentionally exposes only the
features the bring-up path needs, but vkmark requests samplerAnisotropy
unconditionally at device creation.  The hardware supports anisotropic
filtering, so advertise it for chip 5 as well; this lets vkmark create a
device and run its rendering benchmarks.

Signed-off-by: Kulesha Evgeniy <voovdop@gmail.com>
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
index 1edffac..0883a04 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
@@ -457,6 +457,10 @@ tu_get_features(struct tu_physical_device *pdevice,
        */
       features->robustBufferAccess = true;
       features->shaderInt64 = true;
+      /* vkmark requests this feature even when it does not sample
+       * anisotropically; the hardware supports it.
+       */
+      features->samplerAnisotropy = true;
       return;
    }
 
